---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import SampleComponent from "@components/SampleComponent.astro";
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import AstroLogo from "@assets/images/astro-logo-light-gradient.png";
import { Content as SampleMarkdown } from "@content/sample-markdown.md";
import Header from "@components/Header.astro"
import HeaderMobile from "@components/HeaderMobile.astro"
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro"
import LargePin from "@components/largepin.astro"
---

<Layout title="Web Design">
  <Container>

  <Header/>
  <HeaderMobile/>
  <div class="page">

<h1>Web Design</h1>
<div class="content1 project-row">

<div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/chet-large.webp" alt='"The Chet Show" Thesis Site' link="/web-design/chet" />
</div>

<div class="text">
  <h2>"The Chet Show" Thesis Site</h2>

<p class="year">(2026)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s 2026 Thesis.</p><p>

“The Chet Show” was a rounchy college-comedy short film series that I had created alongside my good friend Candice Leach. The project was a very fun experience and had a very high production value.</p><p>For my thesis I decided to document this project through my knowledge of web design.  Specifically due to the large scope of the series and how the skills I utilized to manage it all were learnt more from my years of doing design work.</p><p>
In the end <a href="https://thechetshow.com" >thechetshow.com</a> ended up being the largest website I had ever developed up until this point. Utilizing all the content and design skills I had built up until this point, I was able to create a website that acts as a truly memorable user experience.
</p>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="content1 project-row">
  <div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/uup-large.webp" alt="New Paltz UUP Website" link="/web-design/uup" />
  </div> 
  <div class="text">
<h2>New Paltz UUP Website</h2>
<p class="year">(2025)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Fall 2025 Client Design Course.</p><p>I was assigned as an Intern for the UUP’s New Paltz branch. In this role I was tasked to rebuild the New Paltz branch’s wordpress site.</p><p>
By the end of the project I had completely rebuilt the website from the ground up, bringing it into the modern era of wordpress. as well as updating the site to be usable on mobile devices.</p><p>
Some of my favorite aspects I built into the new site was implementing mail chimp implementation and improving the workflow from google calendar to the website, creating a more self-sufficient website that operates more freely with less direct involvement from moderators.
</p>
  </div> </div>

<div class="content1 project-row">

<div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/launch-large.webp" alt="A Direct Link to My Launch Page" link="https://launch.michaellosquadro.com" />
</div>

<div class="text">
  <h2>My Launch Page <span class="direct-link-note">(direct link)</span></h2>

<p class="year">(2025)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Fall 2025 Web Design 2 course. This launch page was built to act as a small highway, linking together all of my congruent projects and websites. Going for a very simple aesthetic, this was primarily used as a playground for some javascript functionality. Make sure to check out this site on desktop for some fun interactive visuals!
</p>
  </div>

</div>


  <div class="content1 project-row">
  <div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/hotw-large.webp" alt="History of the Web" link="/web-design/hotw" />
  </div>
  <div class="text">
<h2>History of the Web</h2>
<p class="year">(2024)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Spring 2024 Web Design 1 course.

History of the Web is a guided tour through the internet, hosted by everyone’s favorite artificial personality HostBot! This was the first website I had ever built, a great learning experiece that was very ambitious at the time. The project was recently updated to work on desktop, as it was originally built for mobile devices exclusively. 
</p>
  </div></div>

<div class="content1 project-row">
  <div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/chami-large.webp" alt="Chami" link="/web-design/chami" />
  </div>
  <div class="text">
<h2>Chami</h2>
<p class="year">(2022)</p>

<p>

Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Fall 2022 Visual Language course.
Chami is an online messenger app concept created for the 2022 Visual Language course offered at SUNY New Paltz. The project focused around creating a fun and interesting brand as well as some mockups for a few of the app's pages.
</p>
  </div></div>


</div>
  
</div>

  </div>
  <Footer/>

  </Container>
  </Layout>


  <style>
.page{
  flex-direction: column;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center
}

.content1{
display: flex;
flex-direction: row;
flex-wrap: wrap;
padding-top:20px;
justify-content: center;
}

.project-row{
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 600px) minmax(360px, 600px);
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 10px;
}

.project-row .image,
.project-row .text{
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
}

.text{
  max-width:600px;
padding-left:30px;
padding-right:30px; 
}

.text h2{
  margin-bottom: 1px;
  line-height: 1.25;
}

.direct-link-note{
  font-size: 0.7em;
  font-weight: 400;
}

.text .year{
  margin-top: 0;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: 0.92em;
}

.text p{
  margin-top: 0;
  padding-bottom: 20px;
}


@media (max-width: 1250px){
.image{
  padding-left:10px;
  padding-right:10px;
}

.project-row{
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 0;
}

.project-row .text{
  order: 1;
}

.project-row .image{
  order: 2;
}
 .project-row .image{
      padding-bottom: 50px;
    }
}

@media (max-width: 768px){

   

    .text .year{
      margin-top: 5px;
    }
  }

  </style>